    <statement><p>Which is a parametric equation for the curve <m>100 = \left(x-1\right)^{2}+\left(y+2\right)^{2}</m>?</p>
<p><var form="buttons">
<li>
<p><m>c(t) = \left(100\cos\mathopen{}\left(t\right)-2,1+100\sin\mathopen{}\left(t\right)\right)</m></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>c(t) = \left(1+10\cos\mathopen{}\left(t\right),10\sin\mathopen{}\left(t\right)-2\right)</m></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>c(t) = \left(10\cos\mathopen{}\left(t\right)-2,1+10\sin\mathopen{}\left(t\right)\right)</m></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>c(t) = \left(1+100\cos\mathopen{}\left(t\right),100\sin\mathopen{}\left(t\right)-2\right)</m></p>
</li>
</var></p>
</statement>
    <solution><m>(1, -2)</m>.  Using the parametric representation of a circle we get <m>c(t) = \left(1+10\cos\mathopen{}\left(t\right),10\sin\mathopen{}\left(t\right)-2\right)</m>.


</solution>
